From 835bc1a7063d779b59b8c910eea7a1d0b3003c65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:09:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: transfer min/max block sizes through aspect-ratio to
 the inline size

A non-replaced box with aspect-ratio, width:auto and height:auto stretched
to the full available inline size even when max-height capped its block
size, so `aspect-ratio: .7234; max-height: 200px` came out 566x200 where
Chrome gives 145x200 (Mastodon media). Per css-sizing-4 the min and max
block sizes are transferred through the ratio: a stretched automatic inline
size is now clamped by them, and a definite block size gives the inline size
through the ratio (no narrower than min-content) for block containers as
well, not only inline-blocks. Content sizes of boxes with a ratio are
clamped the same way, which fixes floats, inline-blocks and shrink-to-fit
abspos boxes.

The block size from the ratio was only applied on the parallel in-flow
path. Blocks laid out sequentially (any block formatting context with
floats), floats, atomic inlines and abspos boxes without insets on both
block sides now take it too. The helpers live in sizing.rs since all these
paths share them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
